  "title": "A worker that lost its claim can still merge",
  "detail": "After the owned() transaction, mergePullRequest (src/git/repos.ts ~1447) awaits a PR lookup and can retry before it runs `gh pr merge`. If another worker reclaims the entry during that lookup and blocks or re-checks it, the stale worker still merges the unchanged SHA: --match-head-commit checks the SHA, not the land claim, and the heartbeat notices the loss only on its next tick (nominally 10 s, unbounded under an event-loop stall). Re-check ownership synchronously immediately before invoking the merge command (after every await inside mergePullRequest), and abort the worker's signal as soon as a heartbeat or check sees the claim lost. Add a test that reclaims during the pre-merge lookup and asserts no merge command runs."
 },
